  <prompt>Render email per-item CARDS (Reply · Reply All · Forward · Summarize the thread) keyed to the active email; they appear on selection with NO typing (a reactive/local card surface, distinct from the ADR-047 proactive spine). Reply/Reply All/Forward call the task-023 `draft_reply`/`draft_forward` tool then open the composer via task-024's `bodyOverride` (thread preserved). Summarize the thread calls the task-023 `summarize_thread` tool and answers in chat (no composer). Cards suppress when there is no single active email (multi-select / deselect).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React 18 + TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 expertise on the SpaarkeAi ConversationPane; comfortable adding a reactive per-item card surface that stays distinct from the server-initiated notification spine and renders correctly in light + dark themes.</role>
  <goal>Selecting an email surfaces four cards with no typing; Reply/Reply All/Forward auto-draft and open the composer with a preserved thread; Summarize answers in chat; the cards clear when no single email is active.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-09/FR-10 client. The active-item conduit (task 001) carries the active email `{id,type,label}` handle (fed by task 012's email selection emit). This task renders the per-item cards on the existing proactive-card surface in `ConversationPane.tsx` (~:164-167) keyed to that handle — a REACTIVE/local card surface that appears on selection with NO typing (NFR-07: distinct from the ADR-047 server-initiated spine; no new push channel). Per `ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md`, per-item actions on an active item render as CARDS (persistent act-on items), not chips. Card actions: Reply / Reply All / Forward → call task-023's `draft_reply(communicationId, mode)` / `draft_forward(communicationId)` (auto-draft), then open the composer via task-024's `bodyOverride` so the composer opens pre-filled with recipients + Re:/Fwd: subject + auto-draft AND the preserved quoted thread. Summarize the thread → task-023's `summarize_thread(communicationId)` → a plain-narrative chat answer (like a file summary), no composer. When there is no single active email (grid multi-select / deselect / tab-switch away), the cards suppress. Coordinate with notification-spine-r1 (owns the ADR-047 suggestion renderer on the same surface) and the analysis-hub/agreements ConversationPane forks — ConversationPane is a sequential spine.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (proactive-card surface ~:164-167; active-item handle consumer)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailComposeActions/useEmailComposeActions.tsx (openComposer + bodyOverride from task 024)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">The per-item card surface is REACTIVE/local-selection-triggered — it MUST stay distinct from the ADR-047 server-initiated notification spine. No merge, no new push channel. Scope: the card surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA">Per-item actions on an active item render as CARDS (not chips); no code/tool syntax in card labels; hover affordances only on clickable regions; collapse proactive-card stacks behind one disclosure header. Scope: the card UI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens — cards render correctly in light AND dark mode; pointer affordances only on clickable regions. Scope: new card UI states.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Cards key to the `{id,type,label}` handle; content (draft body / thread summary) is tool-fetched by id via 023 — never read from a prompt/tab snapshot. Scope: card data.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-10">Reply/Reply All/Forward MUST open the composer via `bodyOverride` (draft above the reducer-derived quoted thread) — never a whole-body replace. Scope: the reply/forward card actions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope clause: render + wire the cards only. Do NOT re-implement the tools (023) or the composer param (024); do NOT alter the document cards (task 026).</constraint>
  </constraints>
