  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor; trace the proactive-card surface (~:164-167), the active-item handle consumer, and how task-023 tools + task-024 `bodyOverride` are invoked.</step>
    <step order="1">Render four cards (Reply · Reply All · Forward · Summarize the thread) keyed to the active email handle; appear on selection with NO typing; suppress on multi-select/deselect/tab-switch.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire Reply/Reply All/Forward → `draft_reply`/`draft_forward` (023) → open composer via `bodyOverride` (024), thread preserved.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire Summarize the thread → `summarize_thread` (023) → plain-narrative chat answer; no composer opened.</step>
    <step order="4">Keep the surface distinct from the ADR-047 spine (NFR-07); collapse the card stack under one disclosure header per criteria doc.</step>
    <step order="5">Add unit/interaction tests + ui-tests; verify dark-mode rendering.</step>
    <step order="6">npm run build SpaarkeAi; update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Reply card auto-draft + preserved thread"><steps><step>Open the Email tab; select an email (do not type)</step><step>Click the Reply card</step></steps><expected>The composer (SendEmailDialog) opens pre-filled with recipients + a Re: subject + an auto-drafted body AND the quoted previous thread preserved below the draft — no manual typing required.</expected></test>
    <test name="Summarize answers in chat"><steps><step>Select an email</step><step>Click the Summarize the thread card</step></steps><expected>A plain-narrative summary of the thread appears as a chat answer (like a file summary); NO composer opens.</expected></test>
    <test name="Cards suppress on multi-select"><steps><step>Multi-select two emails in the grid, then clear the selection</step></steps><expected>No single active email → the per-item cards are absent (suppressed).</expected></test>
    <test name="Dark mode"><steps><step>Toggle dark mode; select an email</step></steps><expected>The four cards use Fluent v9 semantic tokens and are readable in both light and dark themes; hover affordances only on clickable card regions.</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If rendering the cards requires touching the ADR-047 notification-spine renderer or introducing a push channel to make them appear, STOP and escalate (NFR-07 — reactive must stay distinct from proactive) rather than merging the surfaces. Coordinate ConversationPane edits with notification-spine-r1 and the analysis-hub/agreements forks (sequential spine).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>The proactive-card surface exists in ConversationPane (~:164-167); the tools (023) and composer param (024) exist as deps; the active-item handle (001/012) exists.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — render new cards on the existing surface keyed to the existing handle, invoking existing tools; no new surface or channel.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Email has overview parity but no per-item act-on surface — the per-item Email DoD (select → Reply card → pre-filled composer with preserved thread) cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
