  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Selecting an email surfaces the four cards (Reply · Reply All · Forward · Summarize the thread) with NO typing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-item Email DoD: select email → Reply card → composer pre-filled with recipients + Re: subject + auto-draft AND the preserved quoted thread (via 024's bodyOverride).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Summarize the thread → a plain-narrative chat answer; no composer opens.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cards suppress when there is no single active email (multi-select / deselect / tab-switch away).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cards render as CARDS (not chips), collapse under one disclosure header, and are readable in dark mode (semantic tokens).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the card surface does NOT touch the ADR-047 spine or add a push channel (NFR-07 preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no email content is read from a prompt/tab snapshot — all content is tool-fetched by id (023).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SpaarkeAi builds; unit/interaction tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>FR-09/FR-10 client; per-item→cards per ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md. Depends on 023 (tools), 024 (bodyOverride), 022 (contract metadata). ConversationPane is a sequential spine — sequence with 026/041, commit between. NFR-07 reactive≠proactive is a hard boundary.</notes>
